ersian Church, which attempted to approach Orthodoxy and to which Hnana of Adiabene belonged earlier. The article contains also an overview of Martyrius-Sahdona’s literary heritage.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
